  "description": "Supply chains pause last (D-075 §5, the #74 strand case): the stall_recovery_auto opening with a second fisher (gold and planks seeded for it). At minute 17 five settler houses arrive with no garments yet; upkeep empties the treasury at 17:52. Before D-075 the cascade paused the weaver first (need goods) and the town sat on fish alone. Now the weaver is the island's last running producer of the wool garments the houses consume and the sheep farm the last producer of its wool (the guard is transitive), so the cascade skips both and pauses the wood chain and one fisher; the other fisher, then the last producer of fish, keeps running. The garments fill the houses, taxes rise and the auto-resume chain restarts everything; no command after the opening.",
